---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj33.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Replacing Mandatory Quarterly Reporting" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Minimum Content of a Semi-annual Report" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Consolidated Semi-annual Financial Statements" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Why This Statement Was Reworked So Quickly" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — a Semi-annual Report's Minimum Components" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hub">
      <div class="hub-box">
        <div class="hub-title">ASBJ Statement No. 33 — Accounting Standard for Semi-annual Financial Reporting</div>
        <div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Japan GAAP (J-GAAP) · Issued March 2024 · SUPERSEDED by ASBJ Statement No. 37 (2025) · JPY examples</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout warn callout--centered">SUPERSEDED STATUS: Issued in March 2024, this Statement was reworked into ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Accounting Standard for Interim Financial Reporting) within roughly eighteen months, an unusually short lifespan reflecting rapid refinement following the initial rollout. This poster explains the original 2024 framework and its swift evolution.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a>
      <a href="#s2">2. Scope — Replacing Mandatory Quarterly Reporting</a>
      <a href="#s3">3. Minimum Content of a Semi-annual Report</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. Consolidated Semi-annual Financial Statements</a>
      <a href="#s5">5. Why This Statement Was Reworked So Quickly</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Worked Example — a Semi-annual Report's Minimum Components</a>
      <a href="#s7">7. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Critical Judgments</a>
      <a href="#s9">9. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Statement Mapping</a>
      <a href="#s11">11. Related Standards</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Japan's first move to a reduced statutory reporting frequency</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 33, issued in March 2024, ESTABLISHED semi-annual (second fiscal quarter) financial reporting as the PRIMARY statutory interim reporting obligation for listed companies — the FIRST concrete step in Japan's broader shift AWAY from mandatory FULL quarterly statutory reporting (previously governed by ASBJ Statement No. 12, now largely superseded — see the companion poster) TOWARD a lighter-touch regime.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — Replacing Mandatory Quarterly Reporting</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Listed companies' second-quarter statutory reporting obligation</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applied to LISTED companies previously required to file FULL quarterly reports for the FIRST and THIRD quarters — under this Statement, those FULL statutory quarterly obligations were REPLACED by a SINGLE semi-annual (second-quarter) reporting requirement instead.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Minimum Content of a Semi-annual Report</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A condensed set of statements, broadly parallel to prior interim practice</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A compliant SEMI-ANNUAL report included a CONDENSED Balance Sheet, condensed Statement of Income, condensed Statement of Changes in Net Assets, condensed Statement of Cash Flows, and SELECTED explanatory notes — broadly PARALLELING the general interim reporting principles ALREADY established under J-GAAP's general framework.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>Consolidated Semi-annual Financial Statements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Companion consolidation-specific guidance was needed too</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Preparing CONSOLIDATED semi-annual financial statements RAISED specific procedural questions BEYOND the general interim reporting principles — SUCH questions were addressed through a SEPARATE, dedicated standard (which has SINCE been carried forward and updated as ASBJ Statement No. 38 — see the companion poster).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Why This Statement Was Reworked So Quickly</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Refinement following initial implementation, as part of a broader coordinated package</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Within ROUGHLY eighteen months of its ORIGINAL issuance, this Statement was REWORKED into ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Accounting Standard for INTERIM Financial Reporting) — ISSUED alongside a COORDINATED package of related amendments (ASBJ Statements No. 38, 39, and 40 — see the companion posters). This RAPID evolution suggests the ASBJ used the initial 2024 rollout to GATHER practical implementation feedback, then CONSOLIDATED refinements into a MORE COMPREHENSIVE successor standard SHORTLY afterward, RATHER than treating the ORIGINAL 2024 standard as a long-term, settled framework.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — a Semi-annual Report's Minimum Components</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A condensed set of primary statements</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A listed company's 2024 semi-annual filing</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A listed company, applying this Statement for its FIRST semi-annual reporting cycle under the new regime, prepares its second-quarter report.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The report includes a CONDENSED Balance Sheet AS AT the second-quarter end, a condensed Statement of Income for the HALF-YEAR period, condensed Net Assets and Cash Flow statements, and SELECTED notes — REPLACING what would PREVIOUSLY have been TWO separate full quarterly reports (Q1 and the earlier-style H1 filing) with this SINGLE semi-annual document.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 33 originally required</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Condensed primary financial statements for the half-year period</span>
          <span>Selected explanatory notes on significant events since the last annual report</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement mattered most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Materiality assessment relative to the semi-annual period</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Interim-period estimates carried through from prior general interim reporting practice</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A local reporting-frequency policy choice, not an IFRS divergence</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">As with the SUPERSEDED quarterly regime (ASBJ Statement No. 12), IAS 34 does NOT itself mandate any PARTICULAR reporting frequency — Japan's SHIFT from quarterly to semi-annual statutory reporting reflects a LOCAL regulatory policy choice, not a divergence from a SPECIFIC IFRS requirement.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every semi-annual reporting event landed</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Semi-annual report preparation</span>
            <span>All condensed statements</span>
            <span>Superseded by ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
            <span>Successor standard — Interim Financial Reporting (2025)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 12</span>
            <span>The prior quarterly regime this Statement's introduction began replacing</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Semi-annual report</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A statutory second-quarter interim report, replacing the previous requirement for full quarterly reports in the first and third quarters.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-note">ASBJ Statement No. 33 — Accounting Standard for Semi-annual Financial Reporting · Extended Reference Poster · Self-contained, no internet connection required</div>
</StandardPageLayout>
